 "transform": [
  "One source row per (governor, year) they held office; kept only rows with year in 1976..2016 (the range pres_state_panel.json covers) and state a 50-state USPS code (drops Guam/VI/NMI/PR/AS).",
  "party normalized: \"Democrat\" -> D, \"Republican\" -> R, \"Domecratic-Farmer-Labor\" -> D (source typo for Minnesota's Democratic-Farmer-Labor, the state's national-Democratic affiliate). Everything else (Independent, Independent-Republican, compound mid-term-switch strings, blank) is EXCLUDED, not guessed at.",
  "A state-year with two office-holder rows of DIFFERING normalized party (a mid-year inauguration handoff, e.g. a governor elected in a year whose predecessor is also on record that year) is excluded entirely -- year-only granularity cannot say which one was in office when a presidential race was decided that November. 12 state-years excluded this way, 1976-2016.",
  "11 further state-years excluded for a non-D/R party (Independent governors: AK 1992/2016, ME 1976/1996/2000, MN 2000, CT 1992, MN-R fusion 1980) or an empty/compound party field (ND 2012/2016 blank; LA 1992 \"Democrat, Republican\").",
  "The source itself is incomplete for some state-years: NY and TX have no row at all for 2016 (checked directly, not a filter artefact of this transform) -- both are simply absent from this panel's 2016 slice.",
  "Result: 506 of a possible 550 (50 states x 11 presidential years) state-years, D or R only."
 ],
